Below are Java coding practice questions where:
•	Input is taken using Scanner
•	NO loops (for / while / do-while)
•	Only simple logic, conditions, and operators
•	Suitable for beginners / first-year students

Rules for Students
•	Use Scanner for input
•	No loops allowed
•	Use:
o	if, if–else, else if
o	Arithmetic & logical operators
•	One problem → one main() method


Section A — Number-Based Logic 
1. Even or Odd
Take an integer input and print whether it is Even or Odd.

2. Positive, Negative, or Zero
Take an integer input and determine whether it is positive, negative, or zero.

3. Greatest of Two Numbers
Take two integers and print the greater number.

4. Greatest of Three Numbers
Take three integers and print the largest number using if–else.

5. Leap Year Check
Take a year as input and check whether it is a leap year.

6. Vowel or Consonant
Take a single character input and check whether it is a vowel or consonant.

7. Uppercase or Lowercase
Take a character input and check whether it is uppercase or lowercase.

8. Divisible by 5 and 11
Take a number and check whether it is divisible by both 5 and 11 or not.

9. Swap Two Numbers (Without Third Variable)
Take two integers and swap them without using a third variable.

10. Reverse a Two-Digit Number
Take a two-digit number and print its reverse.

Section B — Mathematical Logic 
11. Simple Calculator
Take two numbers and an operator (+ - * /) and operate using if–else.

12. Check Multiple of 10
Take a number and check whether it is a multiple of 10.

13. Find Last Digit
Take an integer and print its last digit.

14. Find First Digit of a 3-Digit Number
Take a three-digit number and print its first digit.

15. Check Eligibility to Vote
Take age as input and check whether the person is eligible to vote.


Section C — Logical Operators 
16. Pass or Fail
Take marks as input and print Pass if marks ≥ 33, else Fail.

17. Grade System
Take marks and print:
•	A → ≥ 80
•	B → ≥ 60
•	C → ≥ 40
•	F → < 40

18. Triangle Validity
Take three angles as input and check whether a valid triangle can be formed.

19. Check Alphabet, Digit, or Special Character
Take a character input and identify its type.

20. Electricity Bill Logic
Take unit consumption and calculate bill:
•	First 100 units → ₹1/unit
•	Next 100 units → ₹2/unit
•	Above 200 units → ₹3/unit
(Use only if–else, no loops)
	

21. Check Divisibility by 3 or 7
Take an integer and check whether it is divisible by 3 or 7.

22. Check Number is Two-Digit or Not
Take a number and check whether it lies between 10 and 99 (inclusive).

23. Check Number is Three-Digit or Not
Take an integer and check whether it is a three-digit number.

24. Sum of Digits of a Two-Digit Number
Take a two-digit number and print the sum of its digits.

25. Area Calculator
Take length and breadth as input and calculate the area of a rectangle.

26. Perimeter of a Circle
Take radius as input and calculate the perimeter of a circle.

27. Check Number is Perfect Square
Take a number and check whether it is a perfect square
(Use Math.sqrt() only)

28. Temperature Conversion
Take temperature in Celsius and convert it to Fahrenheit.

29. Profit or Loss
Take cost price and selling price and determine profit, loss, or no profit no loss.

30. Absolute Value
Take an integer and print its absolute value.

31. Check Character is Digit or Not
Take a character input and check whether it is a digit (0–9).

32. Check Alphabet Case Using ASCII
Take a character and check whether it is uppercase or lowercase using ASCII values.

33. Next Alphabet
Take a character and print the next alphabet
(Input: a → Output: b)

34. Character is Alphabet or Not
Take a character and check whether it is an alphabet.

35. ASCII Value of a Character
Take a character and print its ASCII value.

36. Check Divisible by 2, 3, and 5
Take a number and check whether it is divisible by 2, 3, and 5 simultaneously.

37. Smallest of Two Numbers
Take two numbers and print the smallest.

38. Salary Bonus Calculation
Take salary as input:
•	Salary ≥ 50,000 → Bonus 10%
•	Salary ≥ 30,000 → Bonus 5%
•	Else → Bonus 2%

39. Triangle Type (Using Sides)
Take three sides and determine whether the triangle is:
•	Equilateral
•	Isosceles
•	Scalene

40. Check Number is a multiple of 100
Take a number and check whether it is a multiple of 100.








41. Harshad (Niven) Number – 3 Digits
Take a 3-digit number and check whether it is a Harshad number
(Divisible by sum of its digits).

42. Automorphic Number (Up to 3 Digits)
Take a number and check whether its square ends with the same digits as the number.

43. Strong Number (3 Digits, No Loops)
Take a 3-digit number and check whether it is a Strong number
(Sum of factorial of digits = number)
(Hint: Pre-calculate factorials using if–else)

44. Duck Number
Take a number and check whether it is a Duck number
(Contains zero but not at the beginning).

45. Palindrome Number (3 Digits)
Take a 3-digit number and check whether it is a palindrome.

46. Spy Number
Take a number and check whether the sum of digits equals the product of digits.

47. ISBN Validity (10-Digit, Fixed Positions)
Take a 10-digit number and check whether it is a valid ISBN
(Use manual digit extraction).

48. Armstrong Number (3 Digits – No Loop)
Take a 3-digit number and check whether it is an Armstrong number.

49. Currency Note Counter (No Loops)
Take an amount and calculate number of:
•	₹2000
•	₹500
•	₹100
•	₹50
•	₹10
(Use division and modulus sequentially)

50. Date Validity Check
Take day, month, year and check whether the date is valid
(Consider leap year logic, no loops)

Section H — Advanced Conditional & Operator Mastery
51. Electricity Bill with Surcharge
Calculate bill with:
•	First 100 units → ₹1
•	Next 100 units → ₹2
•	Above 200 → ₹3
Add 20% surcharge if bill > ₹500.

52. Quadratic Equation Roots Type
Take coefficients a, b, c and determine:
•	Real & distinct
•	Real & equal
•	Imaginary
(Using discriminant)

53. Banking PIN Validation
Take a 4-digit PIN and validate:
•	All digits must be different
•	First digit must not be zero

54. Binary to Decimal (Up to 5 Bits)
Take a 5-digit binary number and convert it to decimal
(No loops allowed)

55. Decimal to Binary (Up to 5 Bits)
Take a decimal number (≤31) and print its binary equivalent
(No loops, use division manually)

Section I — Trick & Edge-Case Problems
56. Same Last Digit
Take three numbers and check whether they have the same last digit.

57. Closest to 100
Take two numbers and print which one is closer to 100.

58. Salary Tax Calculator
Calculate tax:
•	≤ 2.5L → No tax
•	≤ 5L → 5%
•	≤ 10L → 20%
•	Above → 30%

59. Password Strength Checker
Check password validity:
•	Minimum 8 characters
•	At least one digit
•	At least one uppercase letter
(No loops; use fixed index checks)

60. Time Format Validator
Take time in HH MM SS and validate 24-hour format.

